<v Jenri>[西班牙语]

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:40.860
<v Nadia Reiman>Anita's struggling, But Jenri seemed like he was doing just fine. He had chocolate. He was surrounded by toys. The next step was for them to get on a plane to go stay with a relative in another part of the US, while their asylum case was being processed. But it's a small town. There aren't a lot of flights. So they go to a shelter run by Catholic charity, where they can spend the night. When they get there, Jenri is taking in every bit of his mom's attention like a sponge.
<v Nadia Reiman>安妮塔很挣扎，但詹里看起来好多了。他有巧克力。他被玩具包围着。下一步是他们登上一架飞机，去美国其他地方的一位亲戚家住，同时处理他们的庇护申请。但那是一个小镇。航班不多。所以他们去了一家由天主教会经营的收容所，在那里可以过夜。当他们到达时，詹里像海绵一样吸收着妈妈所有的注意力。

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:58.680
<v Jeremy Raff>They're like in a little dorm room at this shelter, and they're just sort of reacclimating. They're like in a bunk bed, just, she's tickling Jenri, they're talking. They're sort of like reacquainting themselves.
<v Jeremy Raff>他们在收容所的一个小宿舍里，他们正在重新适应。他们在一个双层床上，她正在逗詹里笑，他们在说话。他们像是正在重新认识彼此。

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:22.710
<v Nadia Reiman>So there's this thing that happens. In Spanish, there's two ways of saying, I love you. There's te quiero, which means, I little love you. Like, I love you, but it's for things that are not necessarily permanent. And then there's te amo, which is like, I love you, love you, for like, I love you with a capital L, and that's for things that don't ever go away. And you do not throw a te amo around, but you can say like, te quiero, like a little bit is here.
<v Nadia Reiman>有件事很有意思。在西班牙语里，说“我爱你”有两种方式。一种是“te quiero”，意思是“浅浅地爱你”。就像我爱你，但它适用于不一定永久的事物。然后是“te amo”，就像“我深爱你”，带着大写的“L”，用于永不磨灭的情感。你不能随便乱用“te amo”，但你可以说“te quiero”，就像有一点儿在这里。

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:23.930
<v Anita>[SPEAKING SPANISH]
<v Anita>[西班牙语]

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:36.060
<v Nadia Reiman>And so Anita is telling Jenri, she's like, guess what. And he's like, te quiero. And she's like, no, te amo. So she's like no, I really love you.
<v Nadia Reiman>安妮塔在告诉詹里，她说，你猜怎么着。他说，te quiero。她说，不，te amo。所以她是在说不，我真的很爱你。

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:40.080
<v Ira Glass>And he kind of giggles and he's like, te queiro, like, I little love you.
<v Ira Glass>他咯咯地笑着说，te queiro，就像“浅浅地爱你”。

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:41.350
<v Jenri>[SPEAKING SPANISH]
<v Jenri>[西班牙语]

